{"chapter": "obsolete", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0ARG", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-properties-section-fpqc}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cde1b0d93895893c26d5724432b49ed492e1b6da9efef391269c4003b8be272f", "source_text": "The material here was made obsolete by Gabber's argument showing that\nalgebraic spaces satisfy the sheaf condition with respect to fpqc\ncoverings. Please visit\nProperties of Spaces, Section <REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9b1235116b02a153510ec49ec4e36f35a520ae1286a458fb59e8419bf1c41049", "unit_id": "tag:0ARG:p001"}
{"chapter": "obsolete", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ARG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\Mor_S(T, X)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\prod\\nolimits_{i \\in I} \\Mor_S(T_i, X)\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-separated-fpqc}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{lemma}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e8cc949c5d371d836adadba126d2bf380ae9429ea10f8780e857f4f9ef5d6eca", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b594c47527a592167922c125de44c9098dc603e14af53acc315364cf55841cb5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a fpqc covering of schemes over <MATH_0005>.\nThen the map\n<MATH_0006>\nis injective.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9aada1df810e8efe7f351f0dc16a81ca6b82e9efdc0046a9aa248e6e80c14b9f", "unit_id": "tag:03W9:statement"}
{"chapter": "obsolete", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ARG", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-properties-proposition-sheaf-fpqc}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{proof}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e2d4198d499cabef52b9b80292aa676075094cbfb511286ac2c6c829b313c3db", "source_text": "Immediate consequence of\nProperties of Spaces, Proposition\n<REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b676d8b0167d10f3e7ea2fc3a06bf57673eb1eab4f15a48c19be8752e36dc9b1", "unit_id": "tag:03W9:proof-p001"}
{"chapter": "obsolete", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ARG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X = \\bigcup_{j \\in J} X_j$", "MATH_0005": "$X_j$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-definition-Zariski-open-covering}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-sheaf-fpqc-open-covering}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{lemma}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a6aaae4fa3fc1b78fd7c21866e518a49e2bf4dc071d5d7e9e7d027a7920f54de", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8cbbe9fc4d1d3785534beea7bc18aa9ccbdf924af354d6678ba6fb179f54df36", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a Zariski covering, see\nSpaces, Definition <REF_0001>.\nIf each <MATH_0005> satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology\nthen <MATH_0006> satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:37458114c2475cb44ce996a416506110cbd8aa9863e40ef400fdcfad96dd048e", "unit_id": "tag:03WA:statement"}
{"chapter": "obsolete", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ARG", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-properties-proposition-sheaf-fpqc}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{proof}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e2d4198d499cabef52b9b80292aa676075094cbfb511286ac2c6c829b313c3db", "source_text": "This is true because all algebraic spaces satisfy the sheaf property\nfor the fpqc topology, see\nProperties of Spaces, Proposition\n<REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:12db328eadecc1c41cdef0986ba9d3879b7a8a318c258b3140d4738e077f88e5", "unit_id": "tag:03WA:proof-p001"}
{"chapter": "obsolete", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ARG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-sheaf-fpqc-quasi-separated}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{lemma}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fc1d71fdb03746b23c5fe47a9dff734e56f22b92d08b07023fe8b8f0926b2e4b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0cbe24384d492c605d43b6edb7b7356752380ec7207454ec72e6bdbb8def6d83", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nIf <MATH_0004> is Zariski locally quasi-separated over <MATH_0005>, then <MATH_0006> satisfies\nthe sheaf condition for the fpqc topology.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ea08d073724ebcdd27783ea8aeb806f82db12ab8244de7cd46c8dd38d839ad00", "unit_id": "tag:03WB:statement"}
